Among the three candidates, 1result.sql is the only script that

• guarantees FIFO + “smallest batch” selection through an explicit running‑total window ordered by purchase date and lot size,  
• never exceeds the on‑hand quantity, and returns exactly the ordered amounts,  
• stays syntactically clean (no fragile CAST/SUB‑SELECT tricks that could fail) and therefore is the most reliable / simplest correct solution.  

The other two statements either rely on an odd sort that can break the FIFO rule (0result.sql) or contain a brittle correlated sub‑select in ORDER BY that may not even execute in some SQL engines (2result.sql).

```plaintext
1result.sql
